1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:04,790
[Uncle]

2
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:12,217
[Oh Jungse]

3
00:00:12,217 --> 00:00:16,584
[Jeon Hyejin]

4
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:22,100
[Lee Kyunghoon]

5
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:27,870
[Park Sunyoung]

6
00:00:29,283 --> 00:00:33,701
[Lee Sangwoo]

7
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:37,910
[Lee Siwon, Hwangwoo Seulhye]

8
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:45,420
[Uncle]

9
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:51,150
[This is a work of fiction. Any similarity to actual persons, institutions, or events, is purely coincidental.]

10
00:00:53,542 --> 00:00:55,342
Be careful of that man. Okay?

11
00:00:55,342 --> 00:00:57,234
That's him? The pervert?

12
00:00:57,234 --> 00:00:58,818
How did he get out?

13
00:00:58,818 --> 00:01:00,392
He might hear us.

14
00:01:00,392 --> 00:01:03,580
Don't make eye contact, he's crazy.

15
00:01:12,951 --> 00:01:16,030
[Crazy, pervert, molester...]

16
00:01:17,834 --> 00:01:19,718
Get inside.

17
00:01:29,442 --> 00:01:34,170
Since then, uncle went into hiding...

18
00:01:42,034 --> 00:01:45,342
The bluebird disappeared.

19
00:01:47,151 --> 00:01:49,242
And...

20
00:01:56,326 --> 00:02:00,340
So did our teacher...

21
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:06,734
Who'll teach us now that our teacher is gone? Is a new teacher coming?

22
00:02:06,734 --> 00:02:11,550
I don't know, even our school system is changing.

23
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:16,426
Hey, I heard the bluebird was your uncle, not your father.

24
00:02:16,426 --> 00:02:20,125
Your uncle and our teacher dated?

25
00:02:20,125 --> 00:02:25,317
She was fired because of your uncle, right?

26
00:02:25,317 --> 00:02:26,826
Just stay quiet.

27
00:02:26,826 --> 00:02:29,826
Don't defend Jihoo, Minggi will do worse.

28
00:02:29,826 --> 00:02:31,951
How long can you take it?

29
00:02:31,951 --> 00:02:34,150
Teacher isn't here anymore.

30
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:37,726
You can't hide behind your uncle.

31
00:02:37,726 --> 00:02:39,734
Just use that thing.

32
00:02:42,851 --> 00:02:45,942
Always have it ready.

33
00:02:48,742 --> 00:02:51,526
You want to be a loser forever?

34
00:02:52,834 --> 00:02:55,542
You need to live a new life.

35
00:02:58,842 --> 00:03:01,542
Something else disappeared, too.

36
00:03:01,542 --> 00:03:04,851
The cowardly Min Jihoo.

37
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,726
Say whatever you want.

38
00:03:06,726 --> 00:03:09,484
What isn't true, can't hurt me.

39
00:03:09,484 --> 00:03:12,418
Hey! What isn't true?

40
00:03:12,418 --> 00:03:13,925
It's all on the news.

41
00:03:13,925 --> 00:03:17,342
The TV said your uncle was crazy.

42
00:03:17,342 --> 00:03:20,634
If you don't know him, I guess you can believe that.

43
00:03:20,634 --> 00:03:25,518
But you all know what kind of a person he is.

44
00:03:25,518 --> 00:03:27,317
If you trust the TV so much,

45
00:03:27,317 --> 00:03:31,026
look up Super Dream Voice 2 winner J. King.

46
00:03:31,026 --> 00:03:33,018
He's Jihoo's uncle.

47
00:03:33,018 --> 00:03:35,418
It's in the past.

48
00:03:35,418 --> 00:03:38,225
Now he's a perverted renter.

49
00:03:38,225 --> 00:03:41,925
Are you scared that I won't transfer?

50
00:03:41,925 --> 00:03:42,942
What?

51
00:03:42,942 --> 00:03:45,726
You're worried that a renter like me,

52
00:03:45,726 --> 00:03:48,526
is smarter and has better test scores.

53
00:03:48,526 --> 00:03:50,634
Why don't you shut your mouth?

54
00:03:50,634 --> 00:03:53,025
Just hit him, hit him!

55
00:03:53,025 --> 00:03:58,018
All you do is bully people, you can never beat me.

56
00:04:09,242 --> 00:04:11,350
Wow, cool! Have a look!

57
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:13,934
- What?
- Let me see.

58
00:04:16,150 --> 00:04:21,734
♪ Dreams always leave us behind ♪

59
00:04:22,442 --> 00:04:26,730
♪ We try to hold on but they're gone... ♪

60
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:31,030
[Uncle]

61
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:35,980
[EPISODE 5]

62
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:39,042
Where are you?

63
00:04:40,742 --> 00:04:43,317
Oh, there you are.

64
00:04:43,317 --> 00:04:45,134
I have to go take care of something.

65
00:04:45,134 --> 00:04:48,650
I prepared some food, eat okay?

66
00:05:21,201 --> 00:05:24,051
[From: Song Hwaeum]

67
00:05:24,051 --> 00:05:27,250
Yes, I prepared all the printings.

68
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:30,517
Please make sure class goes well without me.

69
00:05:30,517 --> 00:05:34,150
Can you also send me Songhee's study report?

70
00:05:34,150 --> 00:05:37,134
She needs it to fulfill her school days.

71
00:05:37,134 --> 00:05:42,717
Okay, just rest. Figure out your transfer.

72
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:46,851
I'm not transferring, I'm going to the school district.

73
00:05:46,851 --> 00:05:49,651
Don't do anything you'll regret.

74
00:05:49,651 --> 00:05:52,751
They can do worse, just give up.

75
00:05:52,751 --> 00:05:55,250
You can't beat them.

76
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:58,626
Diamond is above the principal.

77
00:06:00,617 --> 00:06:02,217
How great?

78
00:06:02,217 --> 00:06:04,934
We even got rid of the teacher. And Jihoo's dad?

79
00:06:04,934 --> 00:06:09,317
I mean, his uncle? He's been living quietly, too.

80
00:06:09,317 --> 00:06:12,225
That's what you get for messing with us.

81
00:06:12,225 --> 00:06:15,651
But child molestation was too much.

82
00:06:15,651 --> 00:06:18,817
We shouldn't be making things up...

83
00:06:18,817 --> 00:06:21,751
Why are you even taking his side?

84
00:06:21,751 --> 00:06:23,250
Who's side?

85
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:26,526
I just don't want rumors to spread and embarrass us.

86
00:06:26,526 --> 00:06:31,418
Aren't you the best at making up false rumors?

87
00:06:31,418 --> 00:06:33,417
Here we go again.

88
00:06:33,417 --> 00:06:35,526
We didn't completely lie.

89
00:06:35,526 --> 00:06:39,525
Remember how perverted he looked at first?

90
00:06:39,525 --> 00:06:43,142
Did Jihoo's father die? Is she divorced?

91
00:06:43,142 --> 00:06:44,767
Who cares.

92
00:06:44,767 --> 00:06:46,850
Gossip is fun, Sis.

93
00:06:46,850 --> 00:06:48,734
I'm jealous she lives alone.

94
00:06:48,734 --> 00:06:51,050
The only thing I want to throw out, is my husband.

95
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:55,250
If a housewife loses her husband, she goes to poverty.

96
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:56,517
You want to be a renter?

97
00:06:56,517 --> 00:06:59,834
Some people find a better husband and live happily.

98
00:06:59,834 --> 00:07:02,526
Someone like Noeul's father. I could do it.

99
00:07:02,526 --> 00:07:03,934
I'd divorce in a heartbeat.

100
00:07:03,934 --> 00:07:07,134
He's handsome, well mannered, and intelligent.

101
00:07:07,134 --> 00:07:09,918
No, not having a mother-in-law is the most important.

102
00:07:09,918 --> 00:07:12,526
I heard he has buildings and land to inherit.

103
00:07:12,526 --> 00:07:15,517
He, himself is also successful.

104
00:07:15,517 --> 00:07:18,417
Single women in our neighborhood, are all after him.

105
00:07:18,417 --> 00:07:20,442
Even all the divorcees.

106
00:07:20,442 --> 00:07:23,734
His standards are too high though.

107
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:28,334
Yeah, I bet he'll remarry some young woman.

108
00:07:28,334 --> 00:07:30,442
He wouldn't be interested in a divorced lady with kids.

109
00:07:30,442 --> 00:07:34,050
Yeah... That only happens in dramas.

110
00:07:34,050 --> 00:07:37,551
Who's the other guy,besides No-eul's dad.

111
00:07:37,551 --> 00:07:39,250
Here's the food you ordered.

112
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,942
- Thank you.
- Please enjoy.

113
00:07:56,051 --> 00:08:00,010
[Hiring Staff]

114
00:08:02,342 --> 00:08:03,542
Welcome.

115
00:08:03,542 --> 00:08:06,734
Oh, hello. Are you the owner?

116
00:08:06,734 --> 00:08:09,325
What?

117
00:08:09,325 --> 00:08:12,092
I saw the ad outside...

118
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:15,734
Can I work here?

119
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:20,426
I'm a customer...

120
00:08:22,642 --> 00:08:24,842
Excuse me, sir! Can you come out?

121
00:08:24,842 --> 00:08:27,626
- Oh, greetings!
- Hello.

122
00:08:27,626 --> 00:08:29,851
Welcome. Have a seat.

123
00:08:29,851 --> 00:08:33,850
No, she's here for the job.

124
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:36,442
Is that so?

125
00:08:36,442 --> 00:08:40,750
Sorry, I prefer someone younger.

126
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,626
How about the kitchen?

127
00:08:42,626 --> 00:08:47,018
I have my chef license, I can clean, cook, or anything.

128
00:08:47,018 --> 00:08:49,317
I currently run the kitchen.

129
00:08:49,317 --> 00:08:51,434
Well just in case, you can have my number.

130
00:08:51,434 --> 00:08:53,150
No, thank you.

131
00:08:53,150 --> 00:08:55,134
Nice to meet you.

132
00:09:00,542 --> 00:09:05,742
Getting older is upsetting enough as it is...

133
00:09:07,626 --> 00:09:11,918
Will you move following the school change?

134
00:09:12,834 --> 00:09:16,725
Not right away, but before the next half of the year.

135
00:09:16,725 --> 00:09:21,242
We haven't got much, I'm trying to do whatever I can.

136
00:09:21,242 --> 00:09:23,842
Do you want me to look into jobs for you?

137
00:09:23,842 --> 00:09:28,042
No, I don't think I can work in this neighborhood.

138
00:09:28,042 --> 00:09:30,351
The Momvelies?

139
00:09:31,142 --> 00:09:35,651
Everyone's afraid Mombvelies will attack if they hire me.

140
00:09:35,651 --> 00:09:39,242
Working away is hard for me to take care of Ji-hoo.

141
00:09:39,242 --> 00:09:42,542
I heard a restaurant nearby is looking for kitchen staff.

142
00:09:42,542 --> 00:09:46,818
- How's your health?
- I'm an outpatient now.

143
00:09:47,942 --> 00:09:50,718
I got a call.

144
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:03,220
[Uncle]

145
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:06,484
Your uncle is moody like a crazy man, right?

146
00:10:06,484 --> 00:10:08,083
How'd you know?

147
00:10:08,083 --> 00:10:10,292
That's the normal response.

148
00:10:10,292 --> 00:10:14,983
I read Elisabeth Kubler Ross's, "On Death and Dying"

149
00:10:14,983 --> 00:10:18,092
that explains, "the 5 stages of grief."

150
00:10:18,092 --> 00:10:20,092
I'm not, it's not true, seriously not true, a misunderstanding...

151
00:10:20,092 --> 00:10:22,701
First step: denial.

152
00:10:22,701 --> 00:10:24,317
Nope! Nope!

153
00:10:24,317 --> 00:10:25,918
Molester? Nope.

154
00:10:25,918 --> 00:10:28,709
Pervert? No.

155
00:10:29,401 --> 00:10:31,990
Second step: anger.

156
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:37,209
No, it's all my fault.

157
00:10:37,209 --> 00:10:40,130
The third: bargaining.

158
00:10:40,130 --> 00:10:42,550
I'll do better.

159
00:10:43,692 --> 00:10:46,330
Fourth: depression.

160
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:11,000
It's been 9 days and 17 hours since...

161
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,417
16 hours and 24 minutes since I came in this room...

162
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:20,317
Disconnecting from the world. Cut off from all humans.

163
00:11:20,317 --> 00:11:22,983
I, Wang Junhyeok, am in isolation.

164
00:11:22,983 --> 00:11:26,584
I will be a cold dead body soon.

165
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:28,000
The fifth and last stage:

166
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Please get my last message to beanie girl.

167
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:36,559
Acceptance.
I'm sorry, I'm sorry...

168
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:40,083
Teacher, don't ever forgive me...

169
00:11:40,083 --> 00:11:41,809
Uncle?

170
00:11:42,501 --> 00:11:44,492
Oh, the sun light.

171
00:11:45,484 --> 00:11:48,818
Uncle, I'm back from after school studies.

172
00:11:48,818 --> 00:11:51,900
Mom will be late today.

173
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:53,201
Do you hate me?

174
00:11:53,201 --> 00:11:56,109
You've been humiliated, and now the transfer?

175
00:11:56,109 --> 00:11:58,709
Sechan and Mingi are bullying you more now?

176
00:11:58,709 --> 00:12:00,992
I don't care.

177
00:12:00,992 --> 00:12:02,609
Let's go.

178
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:05,900
How'd you change so much?

179
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:08,718
You hate touching.

180
00:12:08,718 --> 00:12:13,384
You said I was dirty, and hated touching me.

181
00:12:14,417 --> 00:12:16,018
You changed.

182
00:12:16,018 --> 00:12:17,792
Tell me.

183
00:12:17,792 --> 00:12:21,118
Is it sympathy? Feeling sorry for me?

184
00:12:21,118 --> 00:12:24,417
Do you live with me because you feel sorry?

185
00:12:24,417 --> 00:12:27,918
We're a family. A family takes care of each other.

186
00:12:27,918 --> 00:12:29,701
Family?

187
00:12:29,701 --> 00:12:31,209
Let's get out.

188
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:34,000
Staying in the dark isn't good for you.

189
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,918
Is that why? I've been hearing things.

190
00:12:36,918 --> 00:12:38,601
- Things?
- Yeah, things.

191
00:12:38,601 --> 00:12:40,417
Yeah, that beeping sound.

192
00:12:40,417 --> 00:12:43,592
I hear that beeping whenever I'm alone.

193
00:12:43,592 --> 00:12:45,918
Beep, beep. It's driving me crazy.

194
00:12:45,918 --> 00:12:48,800
Maybe I am going crazy.

195
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,900
Beep, beep, beep.

196
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:52,301
Wait.

197
00:12:52,301 --> 00:12:55,083
That's weird? I can still hear it. Can you hear it?

198
00:12:55,083 --> 00:12:59,484
Uncle, you're not hearing things. Someone's breaking in.

199
00:12:59,484 --> 00:13:01,401
What? Who?

200
00:13:01,401 --> 00:13:03,292
- Maybe it's that guy.
- Who?

201
00:13:03,292 --> 00:13:06,192
- The guy in the hat.
- The drawing?

202
00:13:06,192 --> 00:13:07,918
The guy who injured me?

203
00:13:07,918 --> 00:13:09,609
That bastard!

204
00:13:09,609 --> 00:13:12,800
He thinks no ones home. Quick, call the police.

205
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,192
Don't worry.

206
00:13:14,192 --> 00:13:15,501
A 4 digit code?

207
00:13:15,501 --> 00:13:18,709
The chances of him getting it right is one out of 25 million.

208
00:13:52,918 --> 00:13:55,918
Got you now! We got you!

209
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:58,751
Stay still, call the police! The police!

210
00:13:58,751 --> 00:13:59,651
You stupid robber!

211
00:13:59,651 --> 00:14:02,442
- I'm not a robber!
- What kind of robber would admit it!

212
00:14:02,442 --> 00:14:04,718
- Call the police!
- Not the police! Please!

213
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,634
I used to live here!

214
00:14:07,634 --> 00:14:10,542
- What?
- I used to live here before you.

215
00:14:10,542 --> 00:14:14,234
- Prove it!
- Yeah, evidence! Prove yourself!

216
00:14:14,234 --> 00:14:16,217
The bathroom sink is cracked!

217
00:14:16,217 --> 00:14:18,717
I was the one who cracked it!

218
00:14:20,334 --> 00:14:25,234
Wait, okay, wait. I need more evidence!

219
00:14:25,234 --> 00:14:29,134
The far-end room has star stickers on the ceiling!

220
00:14:29,134 --> 00:14:30,734
- Is that true?
- Yeah.

221
00:14:30,734 --> 00:14:34,042
It freaks me out when I turn off the lights.

222
00:14:34,042 --> 00:14:37,542
- I can't breathe, I can't...
- What initials are they?

223
00:14:37,542 --> 00:14:40,426
Initials? There aren't any. Just stars...

224
00:14:40,426 --> 00:14:41,751
He didn't fall for it...

225
00:14:41,751 --> 00:14:44,850
I'm really not robbing you, I'm sorry.

226
00:14:44,850 --> 00:14:46,751
I'm sorry I broke in.

227
00:14:54,918 --> 00:14:56,534
Come here!

228
00:14:58,317 --> 00:15:01,326
What? Your just a kid!

229
00:15:01,326 --> 00:15:02,770
How old are you?

230
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:04,740
I'm a freshman in college.

231
00:15:07,217 --> 00:15:11,634
I'm really sorry but, can I use your bathroom?

232
00:15:11,634 --> 00:15:14,051
- Number 1 or 2?
- What?

233
00:15:14,051 --> 00:15:16,134
- Why is that important?
- It's not...

234
00:15:16,134 --> 00:15:18,250
- You know where it is.
- Yes.

235
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:20,942
Well, you better.

236
00:15:27,525 --> 00:15:31,242
- Oh, thank God.
- Shouldn't we call the police?

237
00:15:31,242 --> 00:15:34,625
You don't think he's a robber though?

238
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,876
- Money?
- Yes.

239
00:16:01,876 --> 00:16:04,918
Then why didn't you just say that to begin with?

240
00:16:04,918 --> 00:16:07,125
If I told you, I thought you might steal it.

241
00:16:07,125 --> 00:16:11,034
I should've found it first...

242
00:16:11,034 --> 00:16:12,650
What!

243
00:16:13,592 --> 00:16:17,759
How'd you guess the password?

244
00:16:17,759 --> 00:16:20,083
I watched many times, as your family went in.

245
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:22,375
Hey, that's a huge crime!

246
00:16:22,375 --> 00:16:25,918
You're lucky you met nice people like us!

247
00:16:25,918 --> 00:16:27,450
All right, get out now.

248
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:30,375
Yes, I'm sorry. I'll show myself out.

249
00:16:30,375 --> 00:16:33,751
- Change your password.
- Don't look at it then!

250
00:16:39,876 --> 00:16:41,417
Wait, then...

251
00:16:42,759 --> 00:16:45,392
Is the ultrasound his?

252
00:16:51,751 --> 00:16:52,959
I caught on to begin with!

253
00:16:52,959 --> 00:16:55,876
You did, right? I knew everyone found out!

254
00:16:55,876 --> 00:16:57,918
That's crazy, seriously!

255
00:16:57,918 --> 00:17:02,083
Hey, something came up, I'll be right back.

256
00:17:02,083 --> 00:17:04,859
Sure, Sis, we'll be here.

257
00:17:04,859 --> 00:17:07,059
That's what's important...

258
00:17:14,250 --> 00:17:16,375
Why aren't you in the army?

259
00:17:16,375 --> 00:17:18,883
Life must be good.

260
00:17:18,883 --> 00:17:21,467
You look even better.

261
00:17:23,267 --> 00:17:28,367
Why'd you go into their house?

262
00:17:36,667 --> 00:17:40,959
Why are you returning it? I gave it to your father.

263
00:17:40,959 --> 00:17:45,667
You wanted us to take the money and leave quietly?

264
00:17:48,876 --> 00:17:53,876
You didn't know? That's the deal I made with your father.

265
00:17:53,876 --> 00:18:00,184
